  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「オオキバナカタバミ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AA%E3%82%AA%E3%82%AD%E3%83%90%E3%83%8A%E3%82%AB%E3%82%BF%E3%83%90%E3%83%9F",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 110892235,
      "text": "オオキバナカタバミ は、カタバミ科カタバミ属の多年草。南アフリカ原産で、現在では世界各地の温帯に帰化植物として定着している。葉に紫褐色の斑点が多数見られることで他のカタバミと識別が可能。春先に鮮やかな黄色の花を多数咲かせる。別名キイロハナカタバミ。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Oxalis pes-caprae」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxalis_pes-caprae",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1360332819,
      "text": "Oxalis pes-caprae is a species of tristylous yellow-flowering plant in the wood sorrel family Oxalidaceae. Oxalis cernua is a less common synonym for this species. It is commonly known as African wood-sorrel, Bermuda buttercup, Bermuda sorrel, buttercup oxalis, Cape sorrel, English weed, goat's-foot, sourgrass, soursob, or soursop; Afrikaans: suring; Arabic: hommayda (حميضة)."
    }
  },
